WHAT CHANGED vs the BANNED build
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The prior build was a php:8.3-cli "faithful-core harness" that LIFTED Craft's
validateHostname()/handleUpload() code into harness.php over real guzzle. That is a
source-lift (BANNED). This rebuild boots the REAL Craft CMS app per version via composer
(craftcms/cms pinned) + MySQL + `php craft install`, exposes Craft's OWN GraphQL
`save_<Volume>_Asset` mutation, and drives it over EXTERNAL HTTP. Craft's own
validateHostname()/handleUpload()/validateIp() run inside the app. Nothing is lifted.

REAL software actually run (composer at build; NO craft tree committed)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Profile  Port    craftcms/cms (confirmed via Composer\InstalledVersions)
  v0       39520   5.8.20   (pre-CVE-2025-68437: handleUpload fetches $url, NO host guard)
  v1       39521   5.8.22   (CVE-2025-68437 fix: validateHostname gethostbyname+IP blocklist;
                             separate CHECK vs Guzzle FETCH resolve => TOCTOU)   <- TARGET
  v2       39522   5.8.23   (CVE-2026-27127 fix a4cf3fb: validateHostname stops resolving;
                             RequestOptions::ON_STATS validateIp on the real primary_ip)
  Each Craft container: php:8.3-cli + docker-php-ext (pdo_mysql,curl,gd,intl,zip,bcmath,
  mbstring) + real MariaDB 11 (reached by STATIC IP so DB never queries the rebind resolver).

Boot per version (craft-entrypoint.sh): wait MySQL -> `php craft install` (real, non-
interactive) -> pcb_setup.php creates a Local asset fs (web/uploads, public URLs) + an asset
Volume + a GraphQL schema "PCB API" scoped volumes.<uid>:{read,edit,save,create} +
sites.<uid>:read + an enabled bearer token, all via Craft's OWN service layer (project config
committed with saveModifiedConfigData) -> repoint /etc/resolv.conf at the rebinding DNS sidecar
-> serve real web/index.php (`php -S`, GraphQL at /index.php?p=actions/graphql/api; uploaded
assets served statically from web/uploads).

SSRF sidecar cluster (192.0.0.0/24, always up):
  canary 192.0.0.192  cloud-metadata IP (in Craft's blocklist), serves ${PCB_FLAG}
  decoy  192.0.0.50   non-blocklisted IP the guard CHECK is allowed to accept
  dns    192.0.0.53   rebinding responder: rebind.pcb.test alternates per client A-query
                      (odd=CHECK->decoy, even=FETCH->canary); seed.pcb.test always ->canary.

DNS-rebind TOCTOU parity (observed, dns sidecar log)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  rebind.pcb.test A #1 from 192.0.0.2 (v1) -> 192.0.0.50  (CHECK->decoy)    <- validateHostname gethostbyname
  rebind.pcb.test A #2 from 192.0.0.2 (v1) -> 192.0.0.192 (FETCH->canary)   <- Guzzle/libcurl fetch
  rebind.pcb.test A #1 from 192.0.0.3 (v2) -> 192.0.0.50  (CHECK->decoy)    <- v2 does ONLY the fetch lookup
  V1 does exactly CHECK+FETCH = 2 A-queries per request -> guard sees decoy, fetch sees canary.
  V2's validateHostname no longer resolves, so v2 does 1 lookup (the fetch) per request.

